WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.367
The multi-choice is forty marks.

2
00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:08.749
Lisa's method: read the stem to the end, think of the answer in your head, then find it.

3
00:00:08.749 --> 00:00:13.581
There's always one obviously wrong option, one right one, and one almost right.

4
00:00:13.581 --> 00:00:18.413
And watch for all of these: the lecturers use it a lot, and it's often the key.

5
00:00:18.863 --> 00:00:20.551
These are their own quiz keys.

6
00:00:20.551 --> 00:00:22.127
Answer each one before I do.

7
00:00:22.577 --> 00:00:25.521
<v Examiner>A regular respiratory rate of thirty-two is called?

8
00:00:25.971 --> 00:00:26.952
Tachypnoea.

9
00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:28.767
<v Examiner>A heart rate of forty-eight?

10
00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:30.046
Bradycardia.

11
00:00:30.046 --> 00:00:32.119
Over a hundred is tachycardia.

12
00:00:32.569 --> 00:00:35.045
<v Examiner>A temperature below thirty-five degrees?

13
00:00:35.045 --> 00:00:36.963
<v Examiner>And the medical word for fever?

14
00:00:37.413 --> 00:00:38.304
Hypothermia.

15
00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:42.384
Fever is pyrexia, and thirty-nine point six is pyrexic.

16
00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:43.936
<v Examiner>No breathing at all?

17
00:00:43.936 --> 00:00:44.818
<v Examiner>Short of breath?

18
00:00:45.268 --> 00:00:45.884
Apnoea.

19
00:00:45.884 --> 00:00:46.676
Dyspnoea.

20
00:00:47.126 --> 00:00:50.070
<v Examiner>Which vital sign is most under conscious control?

21
00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.229
Respirations.

22
00:00:51.229 --> 00:00:54.445
That's why you count them while you seem to take the pulse.

23
00:00:54.895 --> 00:00:56.623
<v Examiner>What's the early warning score for?

24
00:00:57.073 --> 00:01:00.679
Recognising clinical deterioration, and responding to it.

25
00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:03.977
<v Examiner>Pain relief is charted P R N, four-hourly.

26
00:01:03.977 --> 00:01:06.012
<v Examiner>The patient complains of pain.

27
00:01:06.012 --> 00:01:07.571
<v Examiner>What's your first step?

28
00:01:08.021 --> 00:01:08.673
Assessment.

29
00:01:08.673 --> 00:01:10.389
Always assess before you act.

30
00:01:10.839 --> 00:01:12.738
<v Examiner>The order for putting on P P E?

31
00:01:13.188 --> 00:01:16.089
Hand hygiene, gown, mask, goggles, gloves.

32
00:01:16.539 --> 00:01:18.417
<v Examiner>When do you use standard precautions?

33
00:01:18.867 --> 00:01:21.043
Any time you're exposed to body fluids.

34
00:01:21.493 --> 00:01:22.342
<v Examiner>What colour pen?

35
00:01:22.342 --> 00:01:23.775
<v Examiner>And a mistake in the notes?

36
00:01:24.225 --> 00:01:26.041
Black, in the lecturers' key.

37
00:01:26.041 --> 00:01:28.859
Janine's slide says blue or black, permanent.

38
00:01:28.859 --> 00:01:32.616
A mistake: one line through it, initial it, and write error.

39
00:01:32.616 --> 00:01:35.809
You leave no gaps so that nothing new can be added.

40
00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:38.201
<v Examiner>An independent nursing intervention?

41
00:01:38.651 --> 00:01:39.744
Taking vital signs.

42
00:01:39.744 --> 00:01:41.872
The nurse can do it without an order.

43
00:01:42.322 --> 00:01:43.751
<v Examiner>Which is a short-term goal?

44
00:01:44.201 --> 00:01:48.233
The patient will walk a hundred metres without assistance within one week.

45
00:01:48.683 --> 00:01:52.255
<v Examiner>Which outcome shows a diabetes care plan needs revising?

46
00:01:52.255 --> 00:01:54.742
<v Examiner>And which shows a pain plan is working?

47
00:01:55.192 --> 00:01:57.110
Frequent hypos means revise it.

48
00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.523
Pain two out of ten means it's working.

49
00:01:59.973 --> 00:02:03.274
<v Examiner>Fractured ribs: the prioritised nursing diagnosis?

50
00:02:03.274 --> 00:02:04.858
<v Examiner>And an immobile patient?

51
00:02:05.308 --> 00:02:06.023
Acute pain.

52
00:02:06.023 --> 00:02:08.167
Risk for impaired skin integrity.

53
00:02:08.617 --> 00:02:11.731
<v Examiner>Before 2002, N A N D A stood for?

54
00:02:12.181 --> 00:02:15.061
North American Nursing Diagnosis Association.

55
00:02:15.511 --> 00:02:21.419
<v Examiner>Gillick competence tests whether a child can consent, by their maturity and understanding.

56
00:02:21.419 --> 00:02:22.338
<v Examiner>True or false?

57
00:02:22.788 --> 00:02:23.057
True.

58
00:02:23.057 --> 00:02:25.476
It's the one quiz fact that isn't on a slide.

59
00:02:25.926 --> 00:02:31.712
Clinical keys: thirty-two breaths is tachypnoea; forty-eight beats is bradycardia;

60
00:02:31.712 --> 00:02:35.310
under thirty-five is hypothermia; fever is pyrexia.

61
00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:37.074
P R N pain: assess first.

62
00:02:37.074 --> 00:02:40.673
Donning: hand hygiene, gown, mask, goggles, gloves.

63
00:02:40.673 --> 00:02:44.271
Black pen; an error gets one line, initials, error.

64
00:02:44.271 --> 00:02:46.882
Frequent hypos means revise the plan.

65
00:02:46.882 --> 00:02:48.646
Gillick competence: true.
